    {
      "id": "mesh_start",
      "text": "1. CALCULATE ALL, THEN INSPECT THE MESHES\nFive synthetic objects; explicit Z/Y/X, 2 x 0.5 x 0.5 micrometres. Extract as Single object, then Split Mesh Objects gives disconnected surfaces separate IDs. Colour, Smooth and Simplify have Auto Recalculate enabled in this saved workflow.",
      "position": [
        0.0,
        -170.0
      ],
      "width": 670.0
    },
    {
      "id": "mesh_identity",
      "text": "2. IDENTITIES, COLOURS AND TWO DISJOINT GROUPS\nSplit uses shared triangle edges; no implicit union. Colour uses Triangle count with Turbo. Volume filtering keeps four objects >= 10 um^3 in one branch and the tiny object in the other. Combine reunites all five without welding or lost colours.",
      "position": [
        1050.0,
        -170.0
      ],
      "width": 670.0
    },
    {
      "id": "mesh_refine",
      "text": "3. COMPARE ORIGINAL AND REFINED GEOMETRY\nSaved settings: Smooth 2 iterations at strength 1; Simplify keeps a target of 10% at aggressiveness 4. Open boundaries stay fixed. These sample-specific settings can change shape and measurements; upstream originals remain available. The 3MF Batch Output only declares an output: Calculate all saves nothing.",
      "position": [
        2450.0,
        -170.0
      ],
      "width": 1000.0
    }
  ],
